    "chunk_size_bytes": 1386,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Speaker, I seek permission to ask this Question relating to a matter of urgent national importance from the Minister of Technology under Standing Order No. 27(2).\n\n2523 2524\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dc0\n\nthe culmination of systemic neglect, technical decay and institutional complacency. While the Sri Lanka Computer Emergency Readiness Team- SLCERT - has described the disruption as an \u201cinternal technical issue\u201d, the absence of transparency and accountability has only deepened public anxiety and suspicion.\n\nOver the past six to ten months, Sri Lanka has faced an unprecedented wave of cyber intrusions, targeting banks, State agencies and financial intermediaries. People of repute like the Chairman of BoI, Mr. Arjuna Herath, was also intercepted. These repeated attacks have shaken public confidence in the country\u2019s ability to protect sensitive personal and financial data. Yet, instead of fortifying defences, there has been an alarming silence from the authorities with no comprehensive cyber audit, national digital risk assessment or unified command structure for crisis response. The latest incident has revealed not just a technological failure, but a failure of governance and foresight."
  },
