    "md5": "93b907e85eff903db2c64d66b325440a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1984,
    "chunk_text": "Over the past six to ten months, Sri Lanka has faced an unprecedented wave of cyber intrusions, targeting banks, State agencies and financial intermediaries. People of repute like the Chairman of BoI, Mr. Arjuna Herath, was also intercepted. These repeated attacks have shaken public confidence in the country\u2019s ability to protect sensitive personal and financial data. Yet, instead of fortifying defences, there has been an alarming silence from the authorities with no comprehensive cyber audit, national digital risk assessment or unified command structure for crisis response. The latest incident has revealed not just a technological failure, but a failure of governance and foresight.\n\nMore than temporary inconvenience, what is at stake is the sovereignty of the nation\u2019s data. The Cloud infrastructure that hosts sensitive records of millions of citizens and thousands of State institutions is now under question. A breach or compromise of this scale could have devastating implications for national security, financial integrity and international confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s digital ecosystem. In an era where cyber warfare and digital espionage have become the new battlegrounds of statecraft, this episode must serve as a national wake-up call.\n\nSri Lanka cannot afford to treat this as a transient technical glitch. It must recognize that its digital government infrastructure is now a strategic national asset requiring the same vigilance, investment and oversight as its physical borders or defence installations do. Parliament, therefore, has an urgent duty to demand full accountability, ensure a comprehensive forensic audit of the Lanka Government Cloud and to establish a National Cyber Security Command Authority with powers to secure, monitor and defend all critical digital assets of the State.\n\nSir, I can understand the situation because this is something new that has happened. But, I thought it was necessary - the Hon. Deputy Minister is technologically"
