    "chunk_index": 53,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "81a966debba9a6e49a9dbcbf265cca7c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1783,
    "chunk_text": "3. How many similar system breakdowns, service disruptions or cyber incidents have occurred in the key government digital platforms over the past 12 months and what lessons have been learnt or corrective measures have been instituted thereafter?\n\n4. What was the total financial and economic loss to the nation as a result of this digital infrastructure collapse, including disruptions to e-Revenue Licences, police clearance certificates and other Government revenue streams?\n\n5. What is the Government\u2019s fallback or disaster-recovery mechanism in the event of such system-wide digital failure? Does Sri Lanka maintain a secure, real-time backup facility either onshore or offshore to safeguard citizen and institutional data?\n\n6. Can the Hon. Minister assure Parliament that all sensitive citizens' and Government data hosted on the Lanka Government Cloud remain intact and uncompromised, and will the Government table a cyber security audit report before this House?\n\nSir, you know that a person of repute like the BoI Chairman Arjuna Herath had his personal information leaked on to social media due to a cybercrime. That happened at a bank and I can name the bank, the Cargills\n\n2525 2526\n\n[\u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0ddc\u0db1\u0ddc\u0dba\u0dcf \u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2025 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0dca\u0db1\u0dad\u0dba\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 23\n\nBank, because they have gone to the Securities and Exchange Commission, mentioning that there has been an invasion into their privacy. So, these are not matter that could be swept under the carpet.\n\n7. What steps are being taken to restore public and international confidence in the security of Sri Lanka\u2019s e-Government systems, particularly given the increasing frequency of cyber attacks on banks, public institutions and digital payment networks in the last six to ten months?"
