    "description": "Hansard of 2025-10-23",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/22641_english_2025-10-23.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-10-23-2025-10-23-0055",
    "chunk_index": 55,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8f4da078214c5b5491d1bea9ae65aaec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2134,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, may I just add one more thing. This was something that we have been trying to achieve from 2015 when I was Minister of Finance, but resistance from government servants retarded the success story. The Eastern European countries have managed to come up with their success story owing to the fact that they digitized their economy. I know the Deputy Minister is a very competent person, and my request to you is, while becoming a digitalized economy, ensure that we fast-track it with proven ability so that we would not suffer in the future.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0dbb\u0d82\u0d9c \u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db1 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0da9\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dd2 \u0dbd\u0dca \u0d86\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0d9a \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d85\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf) (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8e \u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95 \u0bb5\u0bc0 \u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba9 - \u0b9f\u0bbf\u0b9c\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe \u0baa\u0bbf \u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. Eranga Weeraratne - Deputy Minister of Digital Economy) Hon. Speaker, firstly, let me correct the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake about the name of the Ministry concerned. It is the Ministry of Digital Economy.\n\nSir, now, I answer the Question on behalf of the Minister of Digital Economy.\n\n1. This incident has been identified as a technical failure. One of the hard disks reached 100 per cent utilization, which in turn caused a portion of the Lanka Government Cloud system to go offline. This automatic shutdown is a fail-safe mechanism designed to protect system integrity and prevent potential data corruption.\n\nWe have taken immediate steps to restore the online services. Since last Saturday night, the services have been available online and all the issues in the system had been fully resolved.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Minister, in such an environment, one hour is too long. So, imagine the duration it took, 24 hours into seven days. Had it been a cyber attack, would you be happy with the system that exists is my question. I am asking this on behalf of everybody and for national security of this country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-10-23-2025-10-23",
    "num": "2025-10-23",
    "date_str": "2025-10-23",
    "description": "Hansard of 2025-10-23",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/22641_english_2025-10-23.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-10-23-2025-10-23-0056",
    "chunk_index": 56,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "5acc305bdee0b47f7591338bb4844a52",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1874,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Deputy Minister, in such an environment, one hour is too long. So, imagine the duration it took, 24 hours into seven days. Had it been a cyber attack, would you be happy with the system that exists is my question. I am asking this on behalf of everybody and for national security of this country.\n\nNow, I will continue with the Answer.\n\n2. Yes, I confirm that that was a failure in the internal system. There is no evidence of any external cyber intrusion, and at no point during the incident was the security or integrity of the data compromised. Throughout the restoration process, we strictly adhered to the highest standards of data protection and system security. Therefore, thereby no data loss has been reported, and also all the services are currently up and running.\n\n3. Over the past 12 months, there have been no major or prolonged system outages impacting on the critical government digital platforms hosted on the Lanka Government Cloud. However, approximately two months ago, a brief service\n\n2527 2528\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dc0\n\ndisruption occurred due to an issue within one of the network components. That issue was rectified within a couple of hours\u2019 time, getting all the affected services back online. At that time also, there was not any cyber security-related incident reported, but the service restoration and allowing proper access to the services has been done within a couple of hours\u2019 time.\n\nAlso, following that incident, ICTA initiated enhanced monitoring of the previously affected components. We took those lessons learnt as a mechanism to go for the procurement of a new LGC 2.5 so that all the shortcomings available in the current LGC could be addressed."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-10-23-2025-10-23",
    "num": "2025-10-23",
