    "chunk_text": "(ii) \u00b7 Implementing training programmes, organizing workshops and providing resource persons, training materials, Acts et cetera to educate information officers, subject officers and other relevant officials of State Ministries, departments, District Secretariats and Divisional Secretariats.\n\n\u0b86\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bc1 \u0bae\u0bc1\u0b9f\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95 \u0bae\u0bc1\u0b9f\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba4 \u0bae\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bb1\u0baf\u0bc0\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd\n\n\u0b8e\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bae\u0b95\n\n2017 147\n\n2018 251\n\n2019 380\n\n2020 472\n\n2021 495\n\n2022 124\n\n2023 64\n\n2024 112\n\n\u0bb5\u0bae )\n\n308\n\nYear Allocated provisions (Rs.)\n\n2016 -\n\n2017 10,000,000.00\n\n2018 30,000,000.00\n\n2019 1,100,000.00\n\n2020 7,152,000.00\n\n2021 13,000,000.00\n\n2022 -\n\n2023 2,000,000.00\n\n2024 2,000,000.00\n\n2025 5,000,000.00\n\n2661 2662\n\n[\u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0daf\u0dba) \u0db1\u0dd2 \u0daf \u0da2\u0dba\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dda\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2025 \u0d94\u0d9a\u0dca\u0db1\u0dad\u0dba\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 23\n\n\u00b7 Conducting awareness programmes for community organizations, Grama Niladharis, field officers and community-based leaders regarding this Act at the Divisional Secretariat level.\n\n\u00b7 Conducting a wide publicity campaign through electronic and print media to raise awareness among citizens in regard to the right to information.\n\n\u00b7 Creating a training pool among school children covering subjects in Grades 9, 10 and 11, covering Advanced Level subjects and making university student aware.\n\n\u00b7 Taking action to obtain information applications relevant to the Right to Information Act via email.\n\n\u00b7 Training public officials as trainers and maintaining a resource pool to conduct training programmes on the Right to Information Act.\n\n\u00b7 Printing of books related to the Right to Information Act such as the Information Officer\u2019s Manual, Training Methods and Training Modules for Trainers, Information Act Guide and citizen awareness leaflets.\n\n\u00b7 Organizing workshops in all the provincial councils in relation to the Right to Information Act.\n\n(iii) \u00b7 Commission\u2019s rules relating to the Act had been drafted and forwarded for approval of the Commission. They are scheduled to be gazetted once approval is granted.\n\n\u00b7 Updating the prices applicable to payments made for obtaining information."
