    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/22644_english_2025-10-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-10-24-2025-10-24-0074",
    "chunk_index": 74,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d8e2edc83f873244fef6059fabd2dc60",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "The Government of Sri Lanka focused on the opportunity identified by the High Commissioner to \"implement transformative reforms\" with reference to Sri Lanka. Following his visit to Sri Lanka in June this year, the High Commissioner highlighted the \"potential for real change representing all segments of Sri Lankan society\" and the \"genuine openness\" shown by the Government. Therefore, the Government urged the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights - OHCHR - and the Human Rights Council - HRC - to seize this opportunity and provide the necessary space to advance the rights and the well-being of all Sri Lankans through its own national processes.\n\n2729 2730\n\n\u0dcf\u0daf\u0d9c\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0ddd\u0dda\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\nprocesses. To this end, the Government has taken steps to strengthen domestic institutions and mechanisms, ensuring their independence by enhancing financial, human resources and technical capabilities. A decision was taken to establish an Independent Public Prosecutor's Office to further strengthen the delivery of justice. A Committee appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers in May, 2024 is already discussing the establishment of this Office. The Cabinet of Ministers decided on 04th August, 2025, to expand the composition of the Committee and to obtain assistance of an increased number of experts as well as by consulting the views of the general public and the Human Rights Commission of Sri Lanka. A process has been initiated for the establishment of a Truth and Reconciliation Commission and that will be established following consideration of the draft law that has already been proposed and after consultations with stakeholders. However, the Government will continue to work in close cooperation with the international community, especially for capacity-building and to obtain technical assistance on mutually agreed areas."
  },
