    "chunk_text": "Then, Hon. Member, with regard to what you raised about the Office for Reparations. I am so glad that you raised it because there appears to be a team, despite the truthful side to it, who are spreading misinformation. For that particular team, I have given three meetings and explained them. First and foremost, the Office for Reparations can only pay up when they are assessed as missing persons. Out of the 16,000 registered, only 4,000 odd had been paid compensation. But remember, payments for missing persons had been made in the 1990s, the early 2000s and right throughout when the Office of Missing Persons was not functioning. According to law, only one-off payment can be made after recognition of the missing person. Somewhere in the 1990s, it could have been Rs. 25,000, in the 2000s, it could have been Rs. 100,000 or Rs. 150,000 and so on and so forth. Now, that team comes to me and requests that all of them be paid Rs. 200,000. In law, there is no provision to pay whatever that was short; there was no such provision. But, I did speak to that particular team who came to see me and told them that I would put that to the Cabinet and get a policy approval for the balance to be paid. However, there is a difficulty in ascertaining the payments made. From the 1990s, those payments were made by various institutions. So, there is no proper record. Therefore, the Government would never know how much each person had received. As a result, I cannot propose a Cabinet Paper in any scientific manner.\n\n2735 2736\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0d9a \u0dc2\u0daf\u0dab\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dba\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0daf\u0da2\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db8\u0daf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0dca\u0dc2\u0db4\u0dda\u0d9a\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dc4\u0dca\u200d\u0daf]\n\n2025 \u0d94\u0dca\u0dc2\u0ddd\u0dca\u200d \u0dcf\u0d9c\u0d9a2.\n\nHon. Rasamanickam, thank you so much for raising that Question and I was able to clarify it.\n\nThen, to answer with regard to the recommendations of the the Constitutional Council, of course, I will leave in the hands of the Hon. Prime Minister."
