    "md5": "71a0eb97e053538e52ea719a73ec66e4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1862,
    "chunk_text": "stabilized. The external sector, including imports and exports, has strengthened even amidst global shocks. Due to the increase in exports, tourism, and foreign remittance inflows, the gross official reserves have exceeded US Dollars 6 billion. It is expected that this year, after almost two decades since 2006, the Government revenue will be able to reach the level of 16 per cent of GDP. It is also expected that the highest primary surplus as a percentage of GDP in its history will be recorded this year, significantly exceeding the target value of 2.3 per cent. Due to these circumstances, we have been able to build strong relationships with international stakeholders and build investor confidence like never before.\n\nThe economic crisis that existed had gradually escalated to an exploding level in the year 2020. This had spread like a domino effect across all sectors of the economy. The end result was that we were declared a sovereign default State in April, 2022. This economic bankruptcy has created a \"lost decade\" for our country. It means that it would take 10 years to reach the economic situation that prevailed before the crisis. Accordingly, many people have predicted that the economic situation in 2019 would be regained in 2029. However, we believe that by the end of 2025, we will be able to regain the economic situation that existed before the crisis.\n\nHon. Speaker, our debt restructuring process is nearly completed. Sri Lanka has been placed on a sustainable fiscal path and the confidence of both domestic and international investors has been further strengthened. These remarkable achievements have led to the country\u2019s sovereign ratings to be upgraded by international rating agencies; Fitch Ratings, Moody\u2019s and S&P to CCC+, Caa1 and CCC+, respectively. These new ratings further reflect investment confidence in Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-07-2025-11-07",
    "num": "2025-11-07",
