    "chunk_text": "Although public servants receive certain concessions under the Agrahara Insurance Scheme currently in operation for public servants, in order to ensure that the benefits provided to employees remaine at a stable level,\n\nwe propose to increase the minimum employee contribution of Rs. 125 by another Rs. 75 and the monthly contributions of Rs. 300 and Rs. 600 by another Rs. 150.\n\nIt is proposed to increase the interest-free festival advance of Rs. 10,000 provided to government employees to Rs. 15,000.\n\n33.8 Distress Loan Advance\n\nIn line with the increase in the salaries of public servants, we have taken steps to increase the amount of the Distress Loan advances they can obtain at an interest rate of 4.2 per cent from Rs. 250,000 to Rs. 400,000. To ensure that these advances can be obtained within a short period of time without any disruption, Rs. 10,000 million has been allocated for the advance account limit of public servants.\n\n33.9 Increase in Allowances for Teachers Engaged in Remote Service and Allowances for Principals\n\nSince the allowances paid to teachers working in schools in remote areas have not been increased for 20 years, we propose to increase the allowance by Rs. 1,500 to motivate those teachers.\n\nIn recognition of the administrative responsibilities and accountability of principals in achieving educational goals, we propose to increase the principal allowance paid to principals serving in the position of principal by Rs. 1,500 and to allocate Rs. 1,000 million to increase the achievement of educational goals.\n\n33.10 Increasing the Allowance of Gatekeepers at Unsafe Railway Crossings"
