    "chunk_index": 34,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "89f0a229c307285df1ce4ad766497d35",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1713,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, when I was Minister of Trade, that particular ratio was in the range of about 70 per cent to the advantage of India and at that time, it was improved to the benefit of Sri Lanka, but still, there is a huge gap that needs to be rectified or corrected to the advantage of Sri Lanka.\n\nWe should be using an upgraded pact to push more value-added exports, have easier access to services and investment in supply chains that create jobs at home.\n\nSir, I wish to ask from the Hon. Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism - I do not see his presence today - the following Questions:\n\n1. Trade Balance Impact\n\nCould the Hon. Minister explain why, despite the Indo-Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement being in force for 25 years, Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to India remained only at US Dollars 884 million compared to the imports of US Dollars 3.76 billion in 2024, an export-to-import ratio of merely 24 per cent, and what corrective measures are planned to close this persistent deficit?\n\n2. Non-Tariff Barriers What steps has the Government taken to address the non-tariff barriers and technical restrictions such as product testing, standards certification and Customs delays that continue to obstruct Sri Lankan exporters from fully utilizing the duty-free access granted under ISFTA? Sir, you could see that owing to imposition of tariff by President Trump, there is a huge potential that exists for us to export our textiles to India because the Indian middle-class population has gone up to about 400 or 500 million. So, there is a huge potential to take advantage of in the short term.\n\n259 260\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dbd\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0dd9\u0dca\u0dad\u0db1]\n\n2025 \u200d\u0db1\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0d9c 08"
  },
