    "chunk_size_bytes": 1128,
    "chunk_text": "In the last Budget, the President spoke about RCEP. That is, Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership with ASEAN and five other countries. He talked about strengthening trade relations with Asia and Africa. Sir, but yesterday, he did not speak a word about the RCEP, did not even mention the term \"RCEP\". Please, tell us whether an iota of work had been done to achieve that objective. The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake just now asked a Question on ETCA. But, there was no answer. Why? Because there is no answer to be given, Sir.\n\nmasses, hoping that God would create jobs for them. God is not going to create jobs for us. Honestly, there had been some 14 rounds of discussions between Sri Lanka and India on CEPA and ETCA. After another two rounds, the agreements could have been concluded. Why on earth are you all dragging your feet? Talking about RCEP is pie in the sky, Madam Prime Minister; it cannot be completed, if you cannot complete ETCA. That is because there is absolutely no way that you all would be willing to liberalize trade in services to even think about RCEP. Some of you all are living in a fool\u2019s paradise."
