    "chunk_size_bytes": 1667,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0db1 \u0dad\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb0\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) Hon. Presiding Member, to preface my arguments on the Second Reading of the Appropriation Bill, I would like to quote from a publication by the ODI, a think-tank, where among the contributors are, former Governor of the Central Bank, Dr.Indrajit Coomaraswamy, Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, the current Governor and also prominent economist Prof. Shanta Devarajan. This book titled \u201cSri Lanka: from debt default to transformative growth\u201d states, I quote:\n\n\u201cThese improvements in the economy can be traced to a combination of decisive stabilisation measures, the IMF programme and interim Indian aid\u2026\u201d\n\nTogether with that, they further say, I quote:\n\nThis was also stated in the IMF Report in 2023. So, all these had taken place before this Government took over; the most difficult job had been completed by the previous administration. This book also states, I quote:\n\n\u201c\u2026Sri Lanka sought bridging finance and aid from India to finance essential imports of food, fuel and medicines. In the first six months of 2022, Indian aid worth $3.8 billion flowed to Sri Lanka, through credit lines and deferred loans and grants. This meant this was India\u2019s largest bilateral aid programme to any country in recent times.\u201d\n\nSo, if not for that, we would have been in dire straits. But, all these things happened before this Government took over. And, now, the Government is continuing to abide by the rules set by the IMF, very obediently following their dictates."
