    "md5": "38f6ca8035fad81884a55f2b3adda5d3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "cent of LTL Holdings without investing a single rupee! How is this happening? This is a very serious matter, Sir. The value of this almost 30 per cent stake is estimated to be between Rs. 34.4 billion and Rs. 64.5 billion, as per independent valuation done by the NDB Investment Bank and the CT CLSA Capital (Pvt.) Limited. Sir, I table* a few documents related to this issue.\n\nWe must demand a full forensic audit of the LTL Holdings and its share transfers, make an immediate referral of this case to the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption and bring in a legislative reform to prevent any future abuse of State-owned enterprises and employee trusts. So, this is not just about recovering stolen billions, but about restoring public trust; it is about sending a message that no one, however powerful he is, can loot the State and walk away unscathed. Therefore, this is a very important exposure.\n\nSir, in the past, we boldly challenged the e-visa scandal taken place during the last regime. We went to the Supreme Court and today, the Controller General of Immigration and Emigration has been punished and is in jail for contempt of court, for not obeying the court order, and the case had been taken up recently. An Hon. Member of the Government pointed it out as if it is their achievement. But, it is us, Members of the Opposition, who went to court and challenged it and finally, got the tender, which was awarded without any transparency and which was to rob the country, cancelled. Almost one-third of the entire IMF bailout would have been earned by them, if we allowed the contract to stand. Therefore, we went to court and challenged it. Of course, the arguments are pending in that case."
  },
