    "chunk_text": "Sir, in the past, we boldly challenged the e-visa scandal taken place during the last regime. We went to the Supreme Court and today, the Controller General of Immigration and Emigration has been punished and is in jail for contempt of court, for not obeying the court order, and the case had been taken up recently. An Hon. Member of the Government pointed it out as if it is their achievement. But, it is us, Members of the Opposition, who went to court and challenged it and finally, got the tender, which was awarded without any transparency and which was to rob the country, cancelled. Almost one-third of the entire IMF bailout would have been earned by them, if we allowed the contract to stand. Therefore, we went to court and challenged it. Of course, the arguments are pending in that case.\n\nHaving said that, Sir, I would now like to deal with some of the other issues they spoke about. For 2026, there is an allocation of Rs. 150 million made for an indoor Sports Stadium in Kalmunai. That same Rs. 150 million was allocated from the Budget of last year, but not a single cent has been spent. That is what the Hon. Kabir Hashim pointed out. So, last year, Rs. 150 million was allocated, but not a single cent has been spent and again, Rs. 150 million has been allocated for 2026. Actually, out of the entire money that had been allocated last year, there has been only a 30 per cent physical progress and not even a 20 per cent financial progress. That is what has happened; that is what the assessment states."
